@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Public test submission — browser state versus durable result
state "Draft ready\nsaved grammar loaded" as Draft
state "Waiting\npendingTest holds UUID/text/grammar" as Waiting
state "Result displayed\npendingTest cleared" as Displayed
state "Completion uncertain\npending request retained" as Uncertain
state "Reload required\ngrammarStale=true" as Reload
[*] --> Draft : public bootstrap and grammar load succeed
Draft --> Waiting : Analyze / allocate UUID unless same pending payload
Waiting --> Displayed : validated response / show exact saved snapshot
Waiting --> Uncertain : Stop waiting, timeout or connection interruption
Waiting --> Reload : HTTP 409 / block further analysis until reload
Reload --> Draft : refresh saved grammar / retain typed text
Uncertain --> Waiting : retry unchanged input/grammar / reuse pending UUID
Uncertain --> Draft : change text / discard pending retry key
Displayed --> Waiting : Analyze again / new UUID, intentional additional test
Displayed --> Draft : edit text / clear displayed result
note right of Uncertain
  Client cancellation stops waiting, not server execution.
  The server may already have inserted the snapshot.
  Refresh Analysis before making assumptions about completion.
  Inspecting a saved test does not clear the unresolved retry key.
end note
note bottom of Displayed
  The durable record has no public update/delete transition.
  Identical request retry returns its existing snapshot;
  request-ID reuse with different text/grammar returns 409.
  Saved tests remain even when this tab reloads or closes.
end note
legend bottom
  Derived logical browser states, not an invented enum or application class.
  Source: frontend/src/FrancAnalyzer.tsx, api.ts, useRequest.ts; persistence: analyzer_history.py/public_access.py.
  Selecting an old snapshot does not rerun it against today's Collection or grammar.
endlegend
@enduml
